  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening capacities of Member States to devise public policy solutions by applying social and human sciences knowledge</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The activity contributes to design and implement the thrust of the Social and Human Science Sector (SHS) by fostering inclusive growth and societies trough a strengthened nexus between knowledge and decision making, with emphasis on supporting public policies that benefit those at the bottom of the income distribution, and those that have been most affected by the crisis. The activity will be structured around social transformation and inclusion policies. It will reinforce capacities to understand better complex interconnected systems and to build resilient and inclusive societies. The promotion of Futures Literacy as a key competence for the 21st century will equip policymakers with strengthened capacities</narrative>
  </description>
